## Context

A web-based e-commerce information system designed to handle end-to-end online buying and selling between sellers and buyers, with dedicated workflows for each operational role involved in fulfilling an order.

## Problem

Managing online orders manually across chat messages and spreadsheets creates friction in tracking inventory, verifying customer payments, assigning couriers, and summarizing sales reports.

## My role

Owner: I designed the multi-role transaction flow, structured the MySQL relational schema (`ecommerce.sql`), built the PHP web application and role dashboards, and containerized the demo for Render deployment.

## As-is analysis

Typical small-scale online selling splits product catalogs, payment proofs, delivery coordination, and sales recaps across disconnected tools. Unifying them into one transactional workflow prevents missed payment checks and stock discrepancies.

## Requirements

- Separate role-based dashboards for Admin, Employee, Courier, and Customer accounts.
- Product browsing, shopping cart management, checkout, and payment confirmation.
- Order management, order history, and detailed order status tracking.
- Inventory management, user administration, and sales reporting for internal staff.

## Solution design

The application separates responsibilities by user role (`admin_dashboard.php`, `employee_dashboard.php`, `courier_dashboard.php`, `customer_dashboard.php`) backed by a shared MySQL database so every order state change updates inventory, payment verification, and delivery views consistently.

## Build

Built with PHP, MySQL, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and Docker (`render.yaml` deployment at `ecommerce1-demo.onrender.com`), covering user registration and management (`manajemen_user.php`), inventory (`inventory_management.php`), cart and checkout (`checkout.php`, `remove-from-cart.php`), payment confirmation (`payment.php`, `confirm-payment.php`), order tracking (`order-management.php`, `order-details.php`, `order-history.php`), and reporting (`report.php`). Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/E-commerce1](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/E-commerce1).

## Verification

Verified end-to-end storefront and back-office flows in the containerized live demo, including user login across roles, cart-to-checkout submission, payment confirmation, and order detail retrieval.

## Outcome

Delivered a working multi-role e-commerce web application with live demo access demonstrating end-to-end order, payment, courier, and reporting workflows.

## Reflection

Separating customer, employee, courier, and admin views early kept each screen focused on the decisions that role actually needs to make.
